 {"id": "LORE-066", "title": "[P4] `validate --execute` persists a 0-check 'lint-verified' history record for the unclassified BUCKET on every run: 225 of 3,161 ledger rows (7.1%) carry no evidence yet claim 'commands parse and answer on the live system'", "status": "pending", "priority": "P4", "created_by": "lore-dogfood-run14", "reasoning": "REPRO at HEAD a6984b4, scratch CWD (no repo state touched):\n  mkdir -p /tmp/probe-e && cd /tmp/probe-e\n  <repo>/.venv/bin/python -m lore validate --class unclassified --execute      # rc=0\n  cat .lore/validate-history.jsonl\n  -> {\"class_id\": \"unclassified\", \"drifted_orders\": [], \"executed_count\": 0, \"honesty_label\": \"lint-verified: commands parse and answer on the live system; this does NOT prove recovery succeeds\", \"outcomes\": [], \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T08:09:51+00:00\", \"total_checks\": 0}\n\nFINDING: `validate --execute` persists one history record per registry entry, including the `unclassified` BUCKET. The bucket has zero checks by construction (LORE-051: it is explicitly NOT a 14th curated class \u2014 audit marks it `\"bucket\": true` in every format), so its record always carries total_checks 0 / executed_count 0 / outcomes [] while its honesty_label still asserts \"commands parse and answer on the live system\". In this repo's own live ledger 225 of 3,161 rows (7.1%) are exactly that record (evidence: docs/qa/evidence/run14/ledger-census.txt, unclassified_rows=225 across 225 batches of 14; batch membership re-verified by grouping timestamps \u2014 the 01:48:39 batch carries all 14 ids including unclassified).\n\nIMPACT: (a) 7.1% of every ledger read is weight carrying no evidence, in a file `lore audit` parses once per class (PERF-2, filed the same run); (b) the record claims lint verification for a run in which no command existed \u2014 the label-overstatement class the LORE-045/050 honesty work removed elsewhere. No functional harm: audit's freshness path reads that record and finds no drift (drifted_orders [] pairs with zero drift outcomes), so the bucket never flips stale.\n\nFIX DIRECTION (one of): do not persist a history record for an entry with zero checks, or keep the row and make its label derive from total_checks (an honest \"0 checks \u2014 bucket, nothing to lint\" instead of the lint-verified claim). Neither may change any curated class's record or the audit row set.\n\nACCEPTANCE: after the fix, `validate --execute` in a scratch CWD either writes 13 records with no `class_id: unclassified` line, or writes the bucket line with a label that does not claim commands answered; `lore audit --format json` still carries the bucket row with `\"bucket\": true` and 13 curated rows byte-identical; a test pins the new shape.\n\nch:trace row=LORE-066 spec=docs/PRD.md#us-3-audit test=none:no-test-covers-bucket-history-row evidence=docs/qa/evidence/run14/bucket-validate-execute-record.jsonl witness=dogfood-run14-local-leg verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:filed-before-fix memory=/dogfood/2026-10-20-lore-run14", "capability_tags": ["python", "verification"], "complexity": 1, "created_at": "2026-10-20T08:14:39.551159+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-22T07:15:00Z", "detail": {}, "foreman_note": "Filed by the lore-dogfood lane, run 14 (2026-10-20), same tick as PERF-2 \u2014 the two rows touch the same file (the bucket row is 7.1% of what PERF-2 measures audit parsing). LORE-051 (bucket distinguished in audit output) is complete and its contract is NOT in question here; this row is scoped to the history-record write path only.", "acceptance_criteria": "ACCEPTANCE (pick branch, state it): in a scratch CWD run lore validate for the unclassified bucket with execution enabled (the selection named in `lore validate --help`), then count the scratch ledger: `grep -c unclassified .lore/validate-history.jsonl` expect (a) 0 new bucket record from that run, or (b) 1 record whose label is the honest zero-checks text with `grep -c 'lint-verified' .lore/validate-history.jso