 {"id": "LORE-063-R2", "title": "[P3] recurrence of LORE-063: skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md:123 read 'expect: 510 passed' while canonical is 523, and `count_sweep.py 523 .` still exits 0 \u2014 the self-reference exemption (count_sweep.py:102-103) exempts the ONE line whose job is to state the count, so this drifted again after its fix", "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "created_by": "lore-dogfood-run14", "reasoning": "RECURRENCE of LORE-063 (closed complete, fix commit 615fda1) at HEAD a6984b4. The row's own title named BOTH halves; only one was fixed.\n\nLIVE REPRO (control box, 2026-10-20):\n  $ .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q | tail -1\n  523 passed in 4.59s\n  $ cat scripts/test-count.txt\n  523\n  $ grep -n 'expect:' skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md\n  123:uv run pytest -q    # expect: 510 passed (count synced to scripts/test-count.txt, LORE-029)\n  $ .venv/bin/python scripts/count_sweep.py 523 .\n  count_sweep_rc=0            # <-- the guard reports CLEAN while the line reads 510 vs 523\n\nMECHANISM (still live, code unchanged): scripts/count_sweep.py:102-103 exempts a whole LINE from the test-count family as soon as `SELF_REFERENCE = \"scripts/test-count.txt\"` appears anywhere in it. The skill's line 123 both quotes the sync file AND asserts a number \u2014 so the one line whose whole purpose is to state the canonical count is the one line the guard cannot check. `count_sweep.py` has not been touched since 3f435ed (2026-09-26, LORE-036); `git log -1 -S'SELF_REFERENCE' -- scripts/count_sweep.py` = 3f435ed, i.e. no fix for the exemption ever landed.\n\nWHY THE CLOSURE DID NOT HOLD: LORE-063's foreman_note reads \"skill line 123 updated 463->510 ... Count guard PASS\". The PASS was the guard's normal output on the exemption it never evaluates \u2014 the number was synced at 510 while canonical was 510, and then 13 tests were added (510 -> 523) and the doc silently rotted again. The drift was caught this run by hand, not by the guard: `count_sweep.py 523 .` returns 0 with the stale literal in place.\n\nRUN-14 ACTION, stated so the fixer is not confused: this dogfood lane corrected the literal on line 123 to 523 (skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md, part of the run's skill update) so the shipped doc is true today. The ROW is scoped to the half that is still broken: the guard exemption that lets any self-referencing line assert a count it never verifies, which is what makes this a recurrence rather than a one-off.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: in `_line_hits`, make the exemption apply only when the line carries NO test-count literal of the family \u2014 e.g. compute the TEST_COUNT_RE matches first and skip the self-reference exemption when any match exists and differs from canonical (or split the path mention from the number by requiring the literal to be followed by a non-parenthetical). Keep CLASS_COUNT_RE handling unchanged. Add a test that a line containing both `scripts/test-count.txt` and a stale `<N> passed` literal produces a hit, and one that the same line with the CANONICAL number stays clean (the exemption must not become a false-positive machine for the canonical file itself, including its own `523` content).\n\nACCEPTANCE: with canonical = `cat scripts/test-count.txt`, `python3 scripts/count_sweep.py <canonical> .` exits 1 and names `skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md:123` when that line states any other number, and exits 0 when it states the canonical number; the two pinned tests above exist in tests/; the LORE-029/LORE-036 families' existing behaviour (dated records allowlisted, threshold phrasing skipped, class count derived) is unchanged.\n\nch:trace row=LORE-063-R2 spec=docs/PRD.md#docs-count-sync test=tests/:count_sweep-exemption-cases(planned) evidence=docs/qa/evidence/run14/count-guard-exemption.txt witness=dogfood-run14-local-leg verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:filed-before-fix memory=/dogfood/2026-10-20-lore-run14 recurrence_of=LORE-063", "capability_tags": ["docs", "verification", "python"], "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-10-20T08:16:23.195471+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T08:16:23.195471+00:00", "detail": {}, "foreman_note": "Recurrence filed by the lore-dogfood lane, run 14 (2026-10-20). Predecessor LORE-063 (status complete, fix 615fda1, created_by lore-dogfood-run12) is byte-untouched by this run; its doc half was re-fixed in-run (literal 510 -> 523 in the same file). THE PREMISE IS NOT THE NUMBER \u2014 it is the guard exemption that hides it, verified directly: `python3 scripts/count_sweep.py 523 .` = rc 0 with the stale literal on disk.", "completed_at": "2026-10-21T17:33:00Z", "commit_hash": "797b590", "guard_result": "PASS", "evidence": "Commit 797b590 (count_sweep.py + 6 doc files + 5 new tests). Gitreins verdict 41fb5874 PASS/COMPLETE. 536 tests pass, ruff clean, count guard PASS."}
-{"id": "LORE-067", "title": "[P3] `lore audit`'s coverage matrix has no incident data path: `runbook_compiled` is the literal `True` (lore/__main__.py:592) and the class list is the literal `SEED_CLASSES` tuple (lore/classes.py:38), so PRD US-3's \"every failure class seen in the last 90 days\" / \"the classes with incidents but no runbook\" and SC-2's \"runs on the fleet's last 90 days of incidents\" are unmet — coverage is a registry size, not a measurement", "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "created_by": "lore-dogfood-run14b", "capability_tags": ["python", "verification"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-20T08:23:15.059112+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-22T07:15:00Z", "detail": {}, "foreman_note": "filed by the dogfood lane (tick lore-dogfood-2026-10-20-08-02-03, second angle 14b) after the same-tick run-14 lane (rows PERF-2/LORE-066/LORE-063-R2, HEAD 6de0660) ceded nothing here: run 14 covered the ledger's cost and the documented install path, this row is the coverage-data-path angle. NOT a duplicate of LORE-064 (P1, freshness signal existed but was unwired; fixed by c63b82d) or LORE-065 (US-4 sync) — grep of the board found no row naming SEED_CLASSES/_CHECKS/a missing incident input. Id minted per family shape: board_next_id.py <board> LORE returns the date-shaped successor LORE-20261009 (this board carries two LORE id shapes), so the small-class successor was grep-confirmed absent in BOTH id shapes (spaced and compact) before the append, and the append script re-asserted it at write time. Evidence: docs/qa/evidence/run14b/.", "reasoning": "GAP: `lore audit`'s \"coverage + freshness matrix\" (PRD US-3) has NO incident input of any kind, and one of its four columns is a constant. The matrix is therefore a report about the shipped registry, not a measurement of the fleet's incidents — so PRD US-3's \"every failure class seen in the last 90 days\" and \"the classes with incidents but no runbook\", and SC-2's \"`lore audit` runs on the fleet's last 