ND file the ingestion capability as its own row. Restating without filing leaves the same gap, one indirection deeper.\n Either way, delete nothing from the honesty prose: `last_validated` must keep reporting `no data` until a human attests.\n\nACCEPTANCE (reviewer's falsifiable test — one of these two must hold, and today neither does):\n (A-branch) With an incident trail containing two classes the registry does not carry, `lore audit --format json` names both as\n     gap rows and `summary.total_classes` exceeds 14; with an empty incident source it reports `incidents_seen: 0` honestly rather\n     than a 14-class coverage claim; and `runbook_compiled` is false for a class the registry lists but `_CHECKS` does not carry\n     (construct one on a scratch registry, which is why this is a test-visible contract and not a demo).\n (B-branch) No sentence in PRD.md US-3/SC-2 (PRD.md:28, PRD.md:63) or README.md:10 claims incident coverage that `lore audit`\n     does not compute; the capability gap has its own row; and README's Shipped bullet still says \"per registry class\".\n\nEVIDENCE: docs/qa/evidence/run14b/audit-no-incident-input.txt (empty-dir vs repo discriminator, raw JSON both sides),\ndocs/qa/evidence/run14b/loci.txt (file:line list + the grep census). Perf note for the fixer: the matrix is cheap today\n(0.11s warm x3, docs/qa/evidence/run14b/timing.txt; PERF-2 already owns the 14x-per-class ledger re-read that this row's\noption (A) must not make worse — wire the incident source ONCE per audit run).\n\nch:trace row=LORE-067 spec=docs/PRD.md#US-3 spec2=docs/PRD.md#Success-criteria-SC-2 wave=none:dogfood-run14b test=tests/:none-covers-audit-incident-coverage doc=README.md#L390 evidence=docs/qa/evidence/run14b/audit-no-incident-input.txt witness=lore-dogfood-run14b-local-leg verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:row-filed-before-fix memory=/dogfood/2026-10-20-lore-run14b", "acceptance_criteria": "ACCEPTANCE (branch A, state it): with an incident trail carrying two 